<h2>How fast can lizards adapt?</h2>
<p>
  Green anoles colonized south Florida from Cuba about 5 to 7 million years ago and
  now live as far north as Tennessee and North Carolina. Our initial work suggests
  that lower thermal limits differ surprisingly little across that range; behavior
  is what differs, with lizards moving into subterranean thermal refugia where air
  temperatures drop below their critical cold tolerance limit. Tropical lizards that
  have arrived in Florida over the past century give us introductions with known
  start dates, allowing us to estimate both the pathways and the rate of
  evolutionary response. Read more in
  <a href="/research/cold-snaps/">what happens to tropical lizards when Florida freezes</a>.
</p>
